[[Open This|How do I find the DHCP range?]]

---

Usually:

# Find the gateway address.
# Open a browser to `http://<gateway-ip>` (for example http://192.168.1.1)
# Log into the router.
# Look for:
#* DHCP Server
#* LAN Settings
#* Network Settings
#Find the DHCP Start and DHCP End addresses.
